<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#undang">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Undang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Undang are the four great territorial chiefs of Negeri Sembilan in Malaysia, ruling the districts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sungai-ujong">Sungai Ujong</a>, Jelebu, Johol and Rembau. Under the matrilineal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adat">adat</a> perpatih customs brought by Minangkabau settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, they hold the right to choose the state's ruler, the Yang di-Pertuan Besar. The arrangement survives in the state's modern constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/undang.jpg" alt="Undang" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The National Archives UK · No restrictions · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CO_1069-491-09_(7888096290)_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
